/* ================= CLV vs. result =================
   ⚠️ SERIES PALETTE AND THEMING — read before "fixing" this.

   The prototype shipped a `@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)` block alongside a
   `[data-theme="dark"]` scope, and the handoff asked for both to be kept. This site does
   not work that way and adding them would BREAK the thing that instruction was protecting.
   Here `:root` IS dark — dark is the default, and light is the override at
   `:root[data-theme="light"]`. There is no OS-preference block anywhere on the site,
   because the theme toggle is the only input. Wire prefers-color-scheme in and a reader
   on a light-OS machine who has chosen Dark gets light series colours on a dark card.
   So the OS setting is ignored here exactly as it is everywhere else on the site, which
   is what "the site's Dark toggle must win over the OS setting either way" actually asks
   for on this codebase.

   The eight series colours are the prototype's, unchanged and validated with the dataviz
   skill's palette checker. Nothing below this block references a raw hex.

   ⚠️ Eight series cannot clear an all-pairs contrast gate — a scatter puts ANY two
   series next to each other, not just adjacent legend slots. The documented mitigations
   are load-bearing and must not be removed: shape is a real channel (eight glyphs,
   assigned so the weakest colour pairs get the most different shapes), selecting a
   player drops the rest to 16%, direct labels in season mode, and the table twin carries
   every value. */
:root{
  --s1:#3987e5; --s2:#d95926; --s3:#199e70; --s4:#c98500;
  --s5:#d55181; --s6:#2fbf3f; --s7:#9085e9; --s8:#e66767;
  --clv-quad:rgba(255,255,255,0.025);
  --clv-band-1:rgba(255,255,255,0.075); --clv-band-2:rgba(255,255,255,0.038);
}
:root[data-theme="light"]{
  --s1:#2a78d6; --s2:#eb6834; --s3:#1baf7a; --s4:#eda100;
  --s5:#e87ba4; --s6:#008300; --s7:#4a3aa7; --s8:#e34948;
  --clv-quad:rgba(43,28,14,0.022);
  --clv-band-1:rgba(43,28,14,0.055); --clv-band-2:rgba(43,28,14,0.028);
}
